#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""vps-tidy: one cleaner for temp files, caches and stray programs on this VPS.

    vps-tidy                       dry run, human report, deletes nothing
    vps-tidy --apply               do the work, SIGTERM then SIGKILL, log every act
    vps-tidy --json                the same report as data
    vps-tidy --only tmp,processes  pick parts: tmp, caches, docker, evidence, processes

The rules are the union of the old host cleaners, each with the safety rule that
came with it. docs/housekeeping-map.md is the map this follows.

Nothing here is scheduled. Any chat runs it from its own loop; every run is
idempotent and safe to run beside another chat's run.

Flags: --root DIR (sandbox), --ps-file FILE (fake process table), --proc-root DIR,
--statvfs-json FILE, --grace SECONDS, --budget SECONDS, --caller NAME.
Env: VPS_TIDY_ROOT, VPS_TIDY_PROC, VPS_TIDY_BOARD_CMD, VPS_TIDY_CALLER.

It never touches ~/.local/state/gh-shared-cache (VSTA-54 owns it), nor git
worktrees, branches or .git (repo-tidy owns them).
"""

